OpenConnect VPN client and its dependency libraries
----------------------------------------------------

Shipped with the Windows build only, installed into `openconnect\` next to the
executable ({app}\openconnect) as `openconnect.exe`, its full transitive DLL
closure, and `wintun.dll`. Windows has no reliable way to obtain openconnect on
a locked-down machine (winget is a non-functional stub on the target Cloud PCs),
so it is redistributed here so the VPN tunnel works turnkey.

  Component : OpenConnect VPN client (upstream https://www.infradead.org/openconnect/)
  Source    : MSYS2 mingw-w64 package `mingw-w64-x86_64-openconnect`
              (upstream openconnect 9.21, released 2026-06-16; the exact version
              redistributed is whatever that MSYS2 package resolves to at build
              time and is logged by the release workflow's
              "Bundle openconnect + DLL closure + wintun" step —
              `openconnect --version`).

OpenConnect is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
(LGPL-2.1-or-later).

The binaries were built by the MSYS2 project. openconnect.exe is accompanied by
its full transitive DLL closure, collected in CI with `ntldd -R` (so a missing
dependency fails the build, not the user). The bundled DLLs are MSYS2 mingw-w64
builds of the upstream libraries below; the exact, definitive file list for a
given release is the set of files present in the installed
`{app}\openconnect` directory.

